    "q-186159": {
      "dom_id": "step-q186159",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following:\n\n$\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{64}{27}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the numbers $64$ and $27$ are both perfect cubes. \n\nSo, to determine the value of $\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{64}{27}},$ we express $\\frac{64}{27}$ as a perfect cube:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{64}{27}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{4}^{3}}{{3}^{3}}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{4\\cdot 4\\cdot 4}{3\\cdot 3\\cdot 3}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{(\\frac{4}{3})}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
