    "q-43337": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43337",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$\\sqrt[3]{-1}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the number $-1$ is a perfect cube.\n\nSo, to determine the value of $\\sqrt[3]{-1},$ we express $-1$ as a perfect cube:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{-1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-1)\\cdot (-1)\\cdot (-1)} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-1)^{3}} & = \\\\ -1 & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
