    "q-171386": {
      "dom_id": "step-q171386",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following:\n\n$\\sqrt[3]{-\\frac{1}{1,000}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the numbers $1$ and $1000$ are both perfect cubes.\n\nSo, to determine the value of $\\sqrt[3]{-\\frac{1}{1,000}},$ we express $-\\frac{1}{1,000}$ as a perfect cube:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{-\\frac{1}{1,000}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{{10}^{3}}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{(-1)\\cdot (-1)\\cdot (-1)}{10\\cdot 10\\cdot 10}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-\\frac{1}{10})\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{10})\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{10})} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{(-\\frac{1}{10})}^{3}} & = \\\\ -\\frac{1}{10} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
